    "reason": "While 因縁 (innen) can mean 'connection' or 'tie' (as per JMdict Sense 1), its most prominent senses often relate to 'fate' or 'destiny' (JMdict Sense 0) or a deep-seated, often karmic, connection. This makes it too specific and nuanced for a general 'tie' (connection/bond) concept, which a core vocabulary item implies. A general language learner would likely expect a more neutral term for 'tie' as a connection.",
